WEBVTT

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.820
Strike out!

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.610
All right!

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.680
Well done, Shigeno!

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.530
Nice pitching!

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.230
<i>He changed the mood of the team...</i>

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.540
<i>all by himself.</i>

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.250
Ball! Ball four!

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.250
Out!

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.240
Foul! Foul!

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.220
Foul! Foul!

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.340
<i>Damn!</i>

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.560
<i>It was just a little bit off!</i>

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.060
<i>Getting cocky? I'll show you!</i>

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.770
<i>I'll tie it up right here!</i>

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.690
Dead ball!

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.600
Shigeno!

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:53.820
Shigeno!

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:04.350
Hey!

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.990
Are you all right, Shigeno?

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.220
Didn't the ball hit you on your dominant hand?

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.910
Show me your hand.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.750
I'm all right.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.030
It only hit the grip.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.130
Grip?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:16.990
Yeah.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:20.500
I pretended to be in pain to trick the umpire.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.550
"Ouch, it hurts!"

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.850
Just kidding.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.260
I see.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.940
Shigeno seems to be all right.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.140
Let's go back.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.850
Don't surprise us!

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.890
<i>Grip?</i>

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:38.370
<i>The ball didn't rebound much, for having hit the grip...</i>

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:49.590
Okay!

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:51.080
There's one out, with runners on first and second!

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.760
It's a perfect chance for us to make a comeback!

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.790
Go! Go! Bats!

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.240
Now hitting, number 2: Kelloge!

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.470
Go for it, Kelloge!

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.000
<i>This bastard...</i>

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.310
<i>Throwing such a dangerous pitch at Shigeno, our pitcher!</i>

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.690
Out!

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.280
Out!

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.070
Dammit!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.300
D-Double play...

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.370
Hey, you! Why are you disappointed?

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.040
Well, no...

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.680
You should be happy about this!

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:30.870
Yeah, yeah!

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.440
No way.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.120
We had such a great chance too...

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.080
He hit it too perfectly, huh?

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.670
Shigeno!

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.560
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:52.890
<i>If they find out about my injury, they'll sub me out!</i>

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.710
Man! That was really unlucky!

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.430
Hey, are you really all right?

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.140
Huh?

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.120
Why?

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.380
Your hand, your hand!

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:06.350
Yeah.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:10.200
I told you, it only hit the grip!

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.900
Sorry,

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:16.470
I wasted the chance you gave us.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:17.890
What are you saying?

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.650
The game isn't over yet.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.230
It's just getting started!

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.450
Yes!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.210
Like Shigeno-kun said!

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:27.730
We just have to defend for the next inning, and then counterattack!

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:28.430
Right?

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.540
Yeah!

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:32.600
I definitely won't allow any runs! Count on me!

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.630
All right!

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.020
Let's do this!

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.040
<i>Damn.</i>

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.190
<i>I don't think anything broke,</i>

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.930
<i>but because of the pain and the numbness, I can't grip properly!</i>

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:56.460
Now hitting, number 12: Morrow!

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.710
<i>He's pretending to be calm,</i>

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.290
<i>but when a pitcher takes a hit to his pitching hand,</i>

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.130
<i>there's no way that it won't have any effect.</i>

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:19.230
Dead ball!

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.980
Nice one, Shigeno!

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.330
He's paying them back immediately after he was hit.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.650
He really knows our style!

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.040
You bastard!

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:30.820
Warning!

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.450
Warning!

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.870
It became a warning game...

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:41.830
So that means they'll stop the game if anyone else does something that seems like retribution?

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:42.840
Y-Yes.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:47.340
Well, they got a warning too, so it's fair.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.830
Why do we get a warning too!?

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:53.260
Just get rid of that clumsy pitcher instead!

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:56.020
You were the ones who hit him first!

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:58.220
Did you say something!?

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.350
N-No.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.440
Now hitting, number 8: Davenport!

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:04.860
Play ball!

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.320
<i>This is odd...</i>

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:11.450
<i>To try to take revenge in such a close game, and with no outs...</i>

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.360
<i>I didn't give him the sign for that either.</i>

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.380
<i>Plus, I don't think Shigeno is the type of guy who would do something like that.</i>

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:20.710
Ball!

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:23.960
Ball two!

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.290
<i>Damn!</i>

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.260
<i>I can't control them!</i>

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.380
<i>As I suspected.</i>

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.640
Ball!

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:39.850
Ball!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.330
Ball four!

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.420
<i>No outs, with runners on first and second, and now Gibson Jr...</i>

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:50.020
<i>This is dangerous.</i>

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:55.160
Sorry about that, my hand slipped a bit.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:07:59.950
That's horrible!

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.220
So that's how it is after all.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.210
You really <i>were</i> hit by the ball, right?

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:06.500
It's nothing.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.460
Of course it is!

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.950
Hurry up and get that looked at!

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:12.940
No way.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.490
I have to beat him.

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:22.180
Even if I was dying, there's no way I'd step down.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.020
However,

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.910
when your hand is injured like that,

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:28.550
can you really keep that man down?

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.860
I don't know.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.640
After all, from the very start...

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:34.990
I never knew if I could beat him.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:37.070
But I have to do something about him anyway!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.310
You're the one who saved this game,

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.960
which we were going to lose.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.590
Do as you want.

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:01.090
Thank you, old man!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.060
We're counting on you, Shigeno!

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:11.480
Now hitting, number 1: Joe Gibson Jr!

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.550
<i>Now that you've lost your precious control,</i>

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:21.510
<i>how will you fight me?</i>

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:28.750
<i>Come on!</i>

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:29.670
<i>Shigeno!</i>

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.510
Ball!

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.300
Ball!

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.640
<i>It's useless, after all...</i>

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.240
You spineless wimp!

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.350
Fight him like a man, you clumsy pitcher!

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:53.860
<i>You're using the effect of the dead ball that hit you as an excuse to walk me?</i>

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.350
<i>Are you afraid of losing our bet,</i>

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.700
<i>and just trying to avoid fighting me!?</i>

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.390
<i>You're boring...</i>

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:03.740
<i>You're really boring, you bastard!</i>

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:04.450
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.500
Ball!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.930
Wait a minute, it's a 0-3 count now!

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:07.950
Ball three!

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:11.210
Hollister!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.830
Call the bullpen!

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:13.840
Yes!

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.310
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.840
<i>I can't control the pitches at all!</i>

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:24.360
<i>What should I do!?</i>

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:27.670
I've got a good feeling about this!

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:32.300
After all, he's an idiot for not being able to dodge a dead ball.

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:34.320
Shi—

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.110
Do your best!

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:40.690
Shigeno!

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:43.400
Just throw it straight down the middle!

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:45.370
Against a lineup like the cowards of the Falcons,

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.460
that'll be more than enough!

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:54.540
<i>Ginumacchi?</i>

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:00.420
Hey, you!

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:01.930
What did you just say?

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:06.810
You've really got some guts to say something like that around us Falcons fans!

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:12.650
<i>In the middle?</i>

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.230
<i>That's right!</i>

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:16.610
<i>That's the only thing I can do!</i>

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.630
<i>In this situation, when my hand is injured and I can't control properly,</i>

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:23.740
<i>even if they'll aim for the middle, this is all I can do!</i>

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:44.600
Strike!

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:48.680
Yes!

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:52.970
<i>What...</i>

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:54.010
<i>was that?</i>

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.610
<i>99 mph!?</i>

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:17.250
This is a free fansub.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:17.250
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:21.670
Strike two!

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.870
<i>W-What's with this speed!?</i>

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:28.010
F-Fast!

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:31.670
Huh? Zero miles per hour?

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:32.890
Is it broken?

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:38.170
No, that's an old model, so it can't show 100 mph or above.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:41.880
So that means it was 100 mph!?

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:43.150
He...

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:46.270
He still had such a fast pitch in reserve!

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:48.390
His limiter has been removed.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.500
Even if you're pitching for real,

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.450
when you control the course of the ball,

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:55.960
your speed will always decrease a little.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:13:01.540
In that limited condition, Shigeno trained all the time...

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:04.380
to pitch faster than 90 mph.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.420
In other words,

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:08.350
if he removes the limiter that he puts on when he's using control,

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:12.350
it's not strange at all that Shigeno's become able to...

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.600
shoot a bullet at the speed of 100 mph!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.410
Foul!

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.480
<i>That Shigeno!</i>

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:31.700
<i>He's throwing some amazing pitches in this situation!</i>

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:34.660
<i>Impossible!</i>

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:44.940
<i>Against a puny fastball straight down the middle,</i>

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:47.870
<i>all I can do is barely hit!?</i>

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:53.600
<i>If you strike me out just once in this series,</i>

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.970
<i>then I will go to Japan...</i>

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:59.150
<i>and put my hands together and apologize in front of your old man's grave!</i>

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:02.460
<i>But in reverse...</i>

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.570
<i>If I hit just one home run off your pitches,</i>

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.070
<i>then you will get out of America immediately!</i>

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:14.970
<i>I will,</i>

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:16.500
<i>even if I have to throw away my pride,</i>

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.920
<i>absolutely not...</i>

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:20.830
<i>strike out here!</i>

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.140
Foul!

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:25.260
That was close!

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:29.090
He changed his grip and made it more compact to get a better swing!

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:53.650
<i>No, wait...</i>

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.960
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.790
<i>He...</i>

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.790
<i>didn't run away in the first at-bat either.</i>

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:05.160
<i>He didn't fear my home run,</i>

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:08.610
<i>but challenged me head-on without hesitation, only intending to strike me out!</i>

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:14.810
<i>In spite of that, when he's challenging me even with his hand hurt...</i>

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.410
<i>what kind of small-minded approach am I taking!?</i>

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.360
<i>I'll hit it!</i>

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.700
<i>I'll use my best swing,</i>

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:27.900
<i>and against his best pitch,</i>

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.200
<i>I'll beat him!</i>

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.490
Strike out!

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:51.590
Yeah!

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:52.880
He did it!

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.720
Yes!

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.730
That was really fast!

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:04.970
Yeah.

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:07.610
He managed to strike out Gibson Jr.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.170
He's good!

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.700
<i>102 mph!?</i>

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.680
<i>It was 164 km/h!?</i>

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:26.590
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:30.350
<i>I've been burdened with having to apologize to his old man.</i>

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:33.620
<i>But...</i>

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:36.010
<i>that doesn't matter at all anymore!</i>

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.880
<i>Honda Jr,</i>

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.890
<i>as long as I don't defeat you,</i>

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:42.440
<i>my door to the Majors won't open!</i>

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:49.080
We somehow managed to get through this...

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:51.110
Hey, it's just one out!

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.800
We can't relax yet.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.840
And besides, next up is the fourth batter—

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:57.660
Strike!

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.660
Strike two!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:16.680
Damn!

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.180
Out!

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.890
Okay! Now it's two outs!

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:35.150
<i>It can't be that his hand is...</i>

00:17:58.650 --> 00:17:59.470
Balk!

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.060
Shigeno!

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:02.550
Shigeno!

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:03.540
What's the matter?

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:07.380
You really hurt your hand after all...

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:10.160
That's odd.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:14.740
I couldn't feel any pain or numbness until Junior's at-bat.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:19.980
Well, I guess this is what "Gaining super-human strength at the scene of a fire" means.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:24.870
However, suddenly all my energy is gone.

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:30.670
Oh well, this should give the next pitcher time to warm up.

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:34.160
Even if I continue to pitch, I'll just cause trouble for you guys.

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:36.190
So I'll be a good boy and step off the mound now.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.330
Shigeno!

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:47.140
We'll win this game for sure!

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:49.400
Leave the rest to us!

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:52.290
Yeah.

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.580
I'm counting on you.

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:57.440
Well done, Shigeno!

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:15.630
Wait!

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:24.070
I won't forgive you if you try to run away after you just won!

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:27.150
Even in the same Majors, you and I are in different leagues!

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:31.270
You have to return here and fight against me again!

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:48.850
For now, put some ice on that!

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:49.950
And get him to a hospital!

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:54.770
It's a tough situation, with second and third loaded...

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:56.730
but try to get through it somehow, Baker!

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:57.540
Yeah!

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:09.350
<i>Geez! Shigeno, acting so rashly!</i>

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:13.900
<i>Even in this country, such baseball idiots are rare.</i>

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.850
<i>He's controlled the game so far...</i>

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:22.150
<i>We can't allow ourselves to lose at this point!</i>

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.450
Shigeno!

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:35.600
Ginumacchi!

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.460
Is your hand all right?

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:41.290
Yeah, it's nothing to worry about.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:43.870
Just a little spit will heal it right up.

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:45.730
I see...

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:47.290
Anyway,

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:48.760
thanks for that.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:54.100
I challenged them by throwing down the middle because of your shout-out.

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:58.460
I need to thank you too.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.690
I recieved courage from you, Shigeno!

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.050
Even if I go back to Japan,

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:03.400
I can do my best!

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.950
Even if I've given up my dream of going to the Majors,

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.490
you'll work hard for my sake too, right?

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:16.210
Yeah, count on me!

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:20.630
See you.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.330
Ginumacchi!

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.640
Don't ever stop playing baseball!

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:42.030
Now hitting, number 8: Davenport!

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:43.190
Do your best!

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.130
Just one more!

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:45.130
Please!

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.440
Do something to get us through this!

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:52.720
<i>Finish them, Baker!</i>

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:56.120
<i>We really don't want to give Gibson Jr. another chance!</i>

00:22:12.530 --> 00:22:13.810
Out!

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:15.520
Game over!

00:22:14.190 --> 00:22:15.530
You did it!

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:16.890
We did it!

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:16.890
Happy victory!

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:18.330
All right!

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:19.100
We did it!

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:20.110
We did it!

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:21.270
Yes!

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:25.650
<i>We kept our promise, Shigeno!</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:34.640
<i>Remember...</i>

00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:37.280
<i>I won't let it end like this, Honda Jr!</i>

00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:14.050
In Japan, the Pennant Race is at its climax,

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:18.850
and furthermore, Toshiya and Mayumura are competing to become the Newcomer King!?

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:20.810
They sure are full of energy!

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.810
I can't lose either!

00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:24.300
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.300 --> 00:24:25.770
Another Final Battle.

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:28.330
Run towards the stage of your dreams!
